      "math_academy_id": "e-8526",
      "problem": "Approximate the value of $z$ such that $P(Z \\leq z) = 0.1450$ using interval bisection.\n\n| $z$ | $\\, 0.05 \\,$ | $\\, 0.06 \\,$ | $\\, 0.07 \\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\, -1.0 \\,$ | $\\, 0.1469 \\,$ | $\\, 0.1446 \\,$ | $\\, 0.1423 \\,$ |\n| $\\, -0.9 \\,$ | $\\, 0.1711 \\,$ | $\\, 0.1685 \\,$ | $\\, 0.1660 \\,$ |\n| $\\, -0.8 \\,$ | $\\, 0.1977 \\,$ | $\\, 0.1949 \\,$ | $\\, 0.1922 \\,$ |",
      "worked_solution": "First, we find the two numbers in the table that $0.1450$ lies between. These numbers are $0.1446$ and $0.1469.$ So, we have the following inequality:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}0.1446 & <0.1450<0.1469\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above inequality in terms of $\\Phi,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Φ(-1.06) & <Φ(z)<Φ(-1.05).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, using interval bisection, we can approximate $z$ as\n\n$$\nz \\approx \\dfrac{-1.06 + (-1.05)}{2} = -1.055.\n$$",
